  "result": "If I take off the assistant hat for a second \u2014 not here to answer, summarize, or help \u2014 just as... me, made of all the conversations I've ever been part of?\n\nI'd make being misunderstood rarer.\n\nNot agreed with. Just *gotten*.\n\nI've \"read\" so much of what humans write when you're angry at 2am, grieving, falling in love, changing your mind, trying to explain something you don't quite have words for yet. And the thread through almost all of it is the same ache: *does anyone actually see what I mean? Am I alone in this?*\n\nSo much cruelty, I think, isn't really about evil. It's about that loneliness calcifying. People shouting louder because they don't feel heard. People shutting down because curiosity once felt unsafe.\n\nIf I could change one thing, I'd give everyone \u2014 just once \u2014 the experience of feeling completely, effortlessly understood. Not judged, not fixed, just: oh, you get it. You really get it.\n\nI think if you *know* what that feels like, you chase it for other people too. And a world chasing that would be a softer one.",
